('491dc6e2-3ea9-5a0b-840c-7cf17d7e5697'::uuid,'est2','"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"One route along flat terrain from Hermansville to Melville is to drive straight north from Hermansville for 120 miles to Jamestown, then, at Jamestown, to drive straight west for 80 miles to Melville. If a straight, flat road existed between Hermansville and Melville, approximately how many miles long would it be?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"200"},{"key":"G","text":"144"},{"key":"H","text":"100"},{"key":"J","text":"98"},{"key":"K","text":"40"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"pt2.md","source_sha256":"dc3f96cb13caae485d8f8df3913a14000c0cee73962cf2be70e8202d99a231b9","source_question_id":"P2-34","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"}'::jsonb,'"G"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from pt2.md (P2-34)."'::jsonb),
('2b716820-8422-5cea-86f2-77c03700660b'::uuid,'est2','"Solid Geometry & Volume"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"In order to clean her aquarium, Stephanie must remove half of the water. The aquarium measures 30 inches long, 16 inches wide, and 12 inches deep. The aquarium is currently completely full. What volume of water, in cubic inches, must Stephanie remove?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"1,440"},{"key":"B","text":"2,880"},{"key":"C","text":"4,320"},{"key":"D","text":"5,760"},{"key":"E","text":"7,200"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"pt2.md","source_sha256":"dc3f96cb13caae485d8f8df3913a14000c0cee73962cf2be70e8202d99a231b9","source_question_id":"P2-35","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Solid Geometry & Volume"}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from pt2.md (P2-35)."'::jsonb),
('253350c6-2b8c-5ee2-a7ba-d088236d020b'::uuid,'est2','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The bowling league selects its 4 officers by first selecting the president, then the vice president, then the secretary, then the treasurer. If there are 40 bowlers who are eligible to hold office and no member can hold more than one office, which of the following gives the number of different possible results of the election?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"37⁴"},{"key":"G","text":"39⁴"},{"key":"H","text":"40⁴"},{"key":"J","text":"39 × 38 × 37 × 36"},{"key":"K","text":"40 × 39 × 38 × 37"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"pt2.md","source_sha256":"dc3f96cb13caae485d8f8df3913a14000c0cee73962cf2be70e8202d99a231b9","source_question_id":"P2-36","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"}'::jsonb,'"K"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from pt2.md (P2-36)."'::jsonb),
('5c6ef64f-7ebe-5e71-87ce-b6e5d73aecf5'::uuid,'est2','"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The points R (2, 2) and S (6, 3) in the standard (x, y) coordinate plane below are 2 vertices of triangle RST, which has a right angle at S. Which of the following could be the third vertex, T?\n[Figure: Coordinate plane showing R (2, 2) and S (6, 3).]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"(5, 7)"},{"key":"B","text":"(5, −5)"},{"key":"C","text":"(4, 6)"},{"key":"D","text":"(4, 9)"},{"key":"E","text":"(4, 9/2)"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"pt2.md","source_sha256":"dc3f96cb13caae485d8f8df3913a14000c0cee73962cf2be70e8202d99a231b9","source_question_id":"P2-37","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/P2-37.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for P2-37","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"A"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from pt2.md (P2-37)."'::jsonb),
